Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: `[Float#3].swizzle` needs at least one constant slot index
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:6:13
    |
  6 |     _a: rgb.swizzle()
    |             ^^^^^^^
 Why: Numeric swizzle selects one or more fixed slots from `[Float#3]` at compile time
 Fix: Pass constant slot indexes in `0..<3`, such as `.swizzle(0)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane

Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: Swizzle index `-1` is out of range for `[Float#3]`
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:7:21
    |
  7 |     _b: rgb.swizzle(-1, 0)
    |                     ^
 Why: `[Float#3]` has 3 slots (`0` through `2`)
 Fix: Use slot indexes between `0` and `2`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane

Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: Swizzle index `3` is out of range for `[Float#3]`
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:8:21
    |
  8 |     _c: rgb.swizzle(3, 0)
    |                     ^
 Why: `[Float#3]` has 3 slots (`0` through `2`)
 Fix: Use slot indexes between `0` and `2`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane

Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: Swizzle slot index must be a compile-time constant integer
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:9:21
    |
  9 |     _d: rgb.swizzle(i, 0)
    |                     ^
 Why: Numeric swizzle selects fixed slots while compiling, so every index must be known at compile time
 Fix: Pass a constant integer between `0` and `2`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane

Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: Can't swizzle `[String#2]` because `String` is not copyable
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:11:15
    |
 11 |     _e: names.swizzle(1, 0)
    |               ^^^^^^^
 Why: Numeric swizzle reads slots by value and may repeat them, so the element type must be copyable
 Fix: Swizzle a fixed array of a copyable type, or move elements explicitly
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane

Error: Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane: `F32x4.swizzle` has no 3-lane result type for `F32`
  --> Tests/UI/swizzle_numeric_invalid.jet:13:12
    |
 13 |     _f: v4.swizzle(2, 1, 0)
    |            ^^^^^^^
 Why: Exact lane swizzles return a legal lane type with the same element type
 Fix: Pass a supported lane count for `F32`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidSwizzleLane
